// VNEW_array_fixed_grow.schema — NEW: the fixed bound grown 4 -> 8
//
// One of the fixed form's versioning rows (docs/FIXED-FORM-VERSIONING-TESTS.md).
// The OLD and the NEW file of this pair differ by EXACTLY the row named above,
// so a case in test/tables/versioning_numbers.cpp can say which change the read
// answered for. `lead` and `trail` bracket the row's field: a mislaid size
// moves a neighbour, and the equality check sees it.
//
// THE ELEMENT IS A NESTED TYPE WITH NONZERO DEFAULTS, and that is the whole
// point of the row. A `[4]int32 -> [8]int32` grow asserting slots 4..7 == 0
// passes under a plain zero fill just as well as under the ELEMENT-DEFAULT
// prefill the bill (docs/FIXED-FORM-BILL-READS-BACKWARD.md §12.6) requires, so
// it cannot tell the two apart. With x = 7 and y = 9 it can: a zero fill reads
// 0, the law reads 7 and 9.

package vnew_array_fixed_grow

fixed table Vec
{
    x int32 = 7
    y int32 = 9
}

fixed table ArrayFixedGrow
{
    lead  uint32 = 1
    vals  [8]Vec
    trail uint32 = 2
}
